{"title":"Omega","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Omega</b> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />) is the last letter of the Greek alphabet. In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring_theory\" title=\"Ring theory\">ring theory</a>, omega is a constant the represents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d559c357897ccaf99cb2822e3d414ac688e871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{\\frac{2i\\pi}{3}}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Omega_ring\">Omega ring</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Omega&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Omega ring\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Omega_ring\" title=\"Omega ring\">Omega ring</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>The omega ring is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring\" title=\"Ring\">ring</a> containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89b1eff0f3fbfadff3a70567be70a97ab2d25b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,-\\omega,1,-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />. It has the interesting property that whenever one item in the ring is taken to any power, another item in the ring is the result.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Other_uses\">Other uses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Omega&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Other uses\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Omega is the smallest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ordinal\" title=\"Ordinal\">ordinal</a> with cardinality <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Aleph_null\" title=\"Aleph null\">Aleph null</a> and the smallest infinite ordinal.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Omega&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring_theory\" title=\"Ring theory\">Ring theory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring\" title=\"Ring\">Ring</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Omega_ring\" title=\"Omega ring\">Omega ring</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040900\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 38/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 70/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 38/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 526/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   30.320      1 Template:Main\n100.00%   30.320      1 -total\n 68.03%   20.628      1 Template:Hatnote\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5643:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040900 and revision id 123911. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}